IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `iana-types`
IMPORT `iana-employment`

-- Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006 (UK) — GOAL 3: THE OFFENCE
-- (ss 21, 22(1)-(1A)).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2006-13.txt.

§ `Goal 3 — the offence`

-- s 21(1) "A person commits an offence if he employs another ... knowing that
-- the employee is disqualified from employment by reason of the employee's
-- immigration status." (1A): employs a disqualified employee and "has
-- reasonable cause to believe" it. (1B): disqualified as in s 15(1). s 22(1)-
-- (1A): a body knows, or has reasonable cause to believe, what a person with
-- responsibility within it for an aspect of the employment does (an input).
@ref ss 21(1)-(1B), 22(1)-(1A)
@export Whether an employer commits an offence under s 21 of the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006 (UK): it employs an adult subject to immigration control who is disqualified by their immigration status, knowing (s 21(1)) or having reasonable cause to believe (s 21(1A)) that they are disqualified. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN e IS AN `Employment facts`  @desc The employment and the employee's immigration position
      o IS AN `Offence facts`     @desc The employer's knowledge or reasonable cause to believe
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under s 21 is committed in` e `with` o IF
        `the employment is contrary to s 15 in` e
    AND (   o's `knew the employee was disqualified`
         OR o's `had reasonable cause to believe it`)

-- s 21(2) "(a) on conviction on indictment— (i) to imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding five years ... (b) on summary conviction— (i) to imprisonment for
-- a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates' court in England
-- and Wales or 6 months in Scotland or Northern Ireland". (4) "In relation to
-- a conviction occurring before 2 May 2022 the reference to the general limit
-- ... shall be taken as a reference to 6 months."
@ref s 21(2)(a)(i)
`the maximum imprisonment on indictment, in months` MEANS 60

@ref s 21(2)(b)(i), (4)
@export The maximum term of imprisonment, in months, on summary conviction under s 21 of the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006 (UK): in England and Wales the general limit in a magistrates' court (6 months for a conviction before 2 May 2022); 6 months in Scotland or Northern Ireland. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence facts`  @desc The jurisdiction, the date of conviction, and the general limit in England and Wales
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment on summary conviction, in months, for` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o's `jurisdiction`
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN
        IF   o's `convicted on` LESS THAN Date 2 5 2022
        THEN 6
        ELSE o's `the general limit in months`
    OTHERWISE 6
